    "hip_far_end": "Second exposure looks up from the street under the transverse eave. From (327,39) to (323,82) the dormer meets the adjoining taller construction. Its yellow-grey edge is distinct from the front black eave. The sloping red hip ridge and its rear end (994,129) in the first image are hidden by the front roof and neighbour in the second.",
    "casement": "Second photograph shows the recess, a pale narrow projecting edge at u293, and only part of the red glazed leaf at 307–323. Yellow fabric obscures its upper panels. The free edge angle and glazing reflections are date-specific and excluded from fixed stonework triangulation."
